An event loop on poll(2)

Valkey's event loop uses event ports, epoll or kqueue, and select(2)
where a system has none of them. Radix has none of them, and select
watches no descriptor of FD_SETSIZE (1024) or more, while the event loop
holds maxclients connections and more: with open files raised to 4096,
the loop is not even made. This adds a poll(2) module, ae_poll.c, which
has no such limit, and has config.h choose it on Radix (__radix__).
The descriptors watched are kept packed in the array poll(2) takes, with
each one's place kept by descriptor, so that a change takes constant time.

